TI  - Treatment of mycoplasma udder infection in cattle with Enrofloxacin (Baytril®)
T2  - TIERARZTLICHE PRAXIS AUSGABE GROSSTIERE NUTZTIERE
AB  - In a large cow stock with serious damage caused by udder infections with staphylococci, streptococci and Mycoplasma californicum the treatment of the mycoplasma infection with Enrofloxacin was carried out as a trial. A three times repeated dose of 5 mg/kg body weight Baytril((R)) 10% at daily interval all of 15 infected lactating cows could be healed bacteriologically and in 73% of them a clinical and functional healing was achieved. In six out of seven dry cows bacterial culture of milk samples was negative for mycoplasma. These results were verified by results at control animals with details about milk production as well as abortion/mortality and new infection rate.
