TI  - EFFICACY AND SAFETY OF TOPICAL TREATMENT WITH HEPARAN-SULFATE IN SUPERFICIAL PHLEBITIS - A DOUBLE-BLIND PLACEBO-CONTROLLED TRIAL
T2  - ACTA THERAPEUTICA
AB  - In order to evaluate the efficacy and tolerability of a cream containing heparan sulfate 1%, a double-blind study vs placebo was carried out in the therapy of superficial phlebitis secondary to orthostatic venous stasis or induced sclerotherapy.  Fifty patients were treated for one month with 2 or 3 applications per day.  After treatment with heparan sulfate 1% cream the objective clinical evaluation and the evolution of symptoms, as reported by patients, showed a statistically significant improvement for all variables except venous ectasis.  The investigator's assessment was clearly in favour of treatment with heparan sulfate cream.
